@page "/patch-notes"
@layout GameLayout
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize]

@if (!Embedded)
{
    <PageTitle>Version 1.0.2 · Path of Boredom</PageTitle>
}

<main class="patch-notes @(Embedded ? "embedded" : null)">
    @if (!Embedded)
    {
        <header class="page-header">
            <a class="back-link" href="./" aria-label="Back to game" title="Back to game"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span></a>
        </header>
        <section class="page-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">LATEST UPDATE</p>
            <h1>Patch Notes</h1>
            <p>Changes and improvements in version 1.0.2.</p>
        </section>
    }

    <article id="version-1-0-2">
        <header class="patch-heading">
            <div class="patch-meta">
                <span class="badge">VERSION 1.0.2</span>
                <span class="badge latest">LATEST UPDATE</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Your achievements, remembered</h2>
            <p>Track your milestones, celebrate each unlock, and keep your account progress across devices.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Update highlights">
                <span>77 achievements</span><span>Account sync</span><span>Menu fixes</span>
            </div>
        </header>

        <section class="patch-section" id="achievements-1-0-2">
            <p class="eyebrow">MILESTONES AND REWARDS</p>
            <h3>Every journey leaves a mark</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Added 77 in-game achievements across the shared game: combat milestones, campaign chapters, class victories and mastery, Endless stages, challenges, relic discoveries, and Ember Camp upgrades.</li>
                <li>Browse locked and unlocked achievements from Account Progression in a dedicated, scrollable list.</li>
                <li>New unlocks display a five-second notification with the achievement name and requirement. Multiple unlocks queue without pausing combat or blocking controls.</li>
                <li>Notifications wait while the app is in the background, support screen-reader announcements, and respect reduced-motion settings.</li>
                <li>Achievements are kept in account progression when signed in. Offline progress stays on the current device or browser until it can sync.</li>
                <li>The final relic-discovery milestone requires all six available relics.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="account-sync-1-0-2">
            <p class="eyebrow">ACCOUNTS AND SIGN-IN</p>
            <h3>Keep what you have earned</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Achievement unlocks are combined during account synchronization so an older profile cannot erase them.</li>
                <li>Older game versions can continue saving account progression without understanding achievements. Existing lifetime-Ember conflict protection remains in place.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="menu-fixes-1-0-2">
            <p class="eyebrow">MENUS AND READABILITY</p>
            <h3>Room for the important details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Fixed horizontal overflow in run menus, including intermission and death reports, by constraining card widths and wrapping long text.</li>
                <li>The achievement list opens separately so it does not crowd the Ember Camp layout on smaller screens.</li>
                <li>The Endless action now distinguishes continuing a victorious campaign character from starting a new Endless run.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </article>

    <article id="version-1-0-1">
        <header class="patch-heading">
            <div class="patch-meta">
                <span class="badge">VERSION 1.0.1</span>
            </div>
            <h2>A smoother, more reliable adventure</h2>
            <p>Highlights from this update include combat balance changes, easier save management, clearer menus, and important fixes.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Update highlights">
                <span>Balance</span><span>Save slots</span><span>Quality of life</span>
            </div>
        </header>

        <section class="patch-section" id="balance">
            <p class="eyebrow">COMBAT AND PROGRESSION</p>
            <h3>A steadier challenge</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Campaign level and Forge damage growth is more measured; the first wave starts with fewer enemies.</li>
                <li>Wave 1 keeps its existing opening difficulty. From wave 2, enemy health and damage now grow more aggressively throughout the campaign, with no fading early-wave bonuses.</li>
                <li>Later campaign waves maintain larger fighting groups and release reinforcements more frequently, so upgraded builds still face pressure.</li>
                <li>Bosses now enter after their reinforcements, when at most two other enemies remain. Their entrance warning and boss music start when they actually arrive.</li>
                <li>Bosses have 90% more health and 20% more damage on top of the stronger wave curve. Enemy stats follow the wave and chosen difficulty, not the upgrades you buy.</li>
                <li>Boss specials repeat a fixed cycle, lock their aim when the warning appears, and keep the full 1.1-second telegraph in every phase. Each of the six bosses gains an extra clearly marked final-phase hazard, with matching visuals and hit detection.</li>
                <li>Endless starts with more Forge upgrades, with tuned opening echoes to keep the veteran start challenging.</li>
                <li>The first 30 Endless echoes use the campaign's rising pressure curve on a veteran baseline. Reinforcements accelerate as you progress, and difficulty continues growing beyond echo 30 without resetting on a new map cycle.</li>
                <li>Early level-ups arrive at a steadier pace. Difficulty choices are now Easy, Medium, and Hard; existing rankings are preserved.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="save-and-fixes">
            <p class="eyebrow">SAVES AND GAMEPLAY</p>
            <h3>Pick up where you left off</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Keep up to five runs and choose a save by its character and run details.</li>
                <li>Fixed saving after choosing a stage challenge, and improved the load, continue, and restart flow.</li>
                <li>Pending reinforcements and bosses are now preserved when saving and loading mid-wave. Existing saves remain supported.</li>
                <li>Fixed movement and dodge controls failing at the start of a run, along with several skill upgrades that did not apply correctly.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="quality-of-life">
            <p class="eyebrow">MENUS AND POLISH</p>
            <h3>Clearer choices across the game</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>The main menu and account options are easier to navigate. Back and restart actions return to the right screen without signing you out.</li>
                <li>Sign in directly from the main menu for cloud saves and rankings, or keep playing offline. Account operations show progress while waiting; browser sign-in sheets can be cancelled.</li>
                <li>Browser and desktop builds use larger menus, clearer Forge cards and a desktop-sized canvas HUD. The Forge notification replaces the extra upgrade banner.</li>
                <li>Browser audio now also unlocks on touch release and click, fixing silent touch sessions. Sound options explain when a gesture is needed to enable audio.</li>
                <li>Skill, Forge, and level-up choices are clearer, with refreshed upgrade cards and arena artwork.</li>
                <li>Run summaries keep their details inside the cards and show when more can be scrolled. Landscape menus fit phone screens better, and gear pickup sounds are quieter.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </article>

    @if (!Embedded)
    {
        <footer>
            <span>Version 1.0.2 · Path of Boredom</span>
            <a href="./">Return to the game</a>
        </footer>
    }
</main>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Embedded { get; set; }
}
